<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- RadarSettingsTab — the Radar tab of the Settings window: what the map DRAWS over the basemap for radar.

       ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
       │  ⌄  Radar sites                                      │
       │    [ ] Show TDWRs                                    │
       │    [ ] Show research radars                          │
       │  ⌄  Home site                                        │
       │    Home site: KTLX · Norman                          │  ← set in the Radar Atlas, not here
       │    [ ] Load home site on launch                      │  ← PERSISTED, default off
       │  ⌄  Readouts                                         │
       │    Distance  [ km | mi | nm ]                        │  ← PERSISTED, app-wide
       │  ⌄  Range rings & ruler                              │
       │    Rings       [x] ── Reflectivity reach             │  ← PERSISTED, default on (the outline)
       │                [x] ┄┄ Velocity reach                 │  ← PERSISTED, default on
       │                [ ] ·· Distance rings                 │  ← PERSISTED, default off
       │    Spacing     [ Auto | 25 | 50 | 100 ]              │  ← in the Readouts unit; greyed while
       │    Ruler from  [ Radar site | My location ]          │    distance rings are off
       │    Colour      (A)(■)(■)(■)(■)(■)(■)                 │  ← A = theme; OUTLINE AND ruler only
       └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

     WHY THIS IS NOT IN THE MAP TAB: these are radar CONTENT drawn over the basemap, and they are GLOBAL —
     one copy for the whole map, not one per pane. The Map tab next door owns the basemap and the camera; a
     control that would need a copy per pane belongs in RadarControls instead.

     ⚠️ THE MILE GRID IS GONE, deleted rather than hidden (its VM, its JS module and its IMapService seam
     with it). It drew a square grid anchored to the selected radar as a distance reference, and it did not
     work: at any opacity that made the lines visible over radar returns they were lost in the basemap's own
     lines, and at any opacity that kept them out of the way they were invisible over returns. A distance
     reference wants a different form — range rings from the site, or a point-to-point measure tool — not a
     grid competing with everything already drawn. Don't re-add this one.
     → THAT DIFFERENT FORM NOW EXISTS: the RANGE RULER (Assets/Map/js/radar-ruler.js), armed from the tools
     tier beside the site picker. It draws ONE cased line instead of a field of them, which is the part the
     grid could not do at any opacity. The unit it speaks in is the Readouts section.

     ⚠️ WHY "READOUTS" IS IN THIS TAB and not the Map tab: the Map tab owns the app's LOOK (theme, basemap),
     and a unit is not a look - it is how a RADAR measurement is spoken, and every consumer of it today is a
     radar instrument. ⚠️ GROUND DISTANCES ONLY: heights and wind-profile layer bounds stay in km whatever is
     picked here, because those are meteorological quantities with a conventional unit (Models/Map/DistanceUnits).

     ⚠️ THE TOOLS SECTION IS GONE with the Inspect toggle — Inspect is a MODE you arm and disarm while
     reading the map, not a setting, so it is a key in the OverlayBar now (MainWindow, InspectKey), on the
     bar's left. It is still a MAP tool rather than a per-pane radar control: one armed cursor over a
     shared camera, reading every pane at one point, with only its VALUE readout per-pane (the live tick on
     each pane's product ramp). That reasoning put it in this tab; being a gesture rather than a preference
     is what took it out again.

     ⚠️ Neither marker toggle affects a LOADED loop — hiding a marker never unloads its data.

     ⚠️ THE MASTER "show site markers" TOGGLE IS NOT HERE ANY MORE — it is a toggle on the tools tier, beside
     the site picker (MapControlsStrip, SitesVisibleToggle). What is left here is the two OPT-IN networks, which is
     the honest split: hiding all markers is a thing you do constantly while reading a busy map, so it wants
     a one-click toggle on the map chrome; choosing whether TDWRs and research radars exist at all is a preference you
     set once. ⚠️ HISTORY, so this is not simply reverted: all three were deliberately put together HERE,
     because with the master toggle on the radar console and the other two in App Settings you had to hunt
     two places for "why is my site gone". That reasoning still holds for the pair, and the tools-tier toggle is
     discoverable in a way a console control was not — but if a third marker toggle ever appears, think hard
     before splitting it off too. -->

<UserControl x:Class="Anvil.Controls.Composites.RadarSettingsTab"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             xmlns:prim="using:Anvil.Controls.Primitives"
             mc:Ignorable="d">

    <!-- Body: one Expander per section (Styles.xaml SectionExpanderStyle), grid rows inside each. -->
    <Grid RowSpacing="8" VerticalAlignment="Top">
        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- radar sites -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- home site -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- readouts -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- range rings & ruler -->
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

        <Expander Grid.Row="0" Header="Radar sites" IsExpanded="True"
                  Style="{StaticResource SectionExpanderStyle}">
            <Grid RowSpacing="8">
                <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Show TDWRs -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- Show research radars -->
                </Grid.RowDefinitions>

                <!-- Opt-in TDWRs (the FAA Terminal Doppler Weather Radar T*** network). PERSISTED. -->
                <CheckBox Grid.Row="0" Margin="4,0,0,0"
                          Content="Show TDWRs"
                          IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.ShowTdwrs, Mode=TwoWay}"
                          ToolTipService.ToolTip="Show FAA Terminal Doppler Weather Radar markers (e.g. TOKC, TDAL)"/>

                <!-- Opt-in research/test radars (e.g. the ROC test bed KCRI). PERSISTED. -->
                <CheckBox Grid.Row="1" Margin="4,0,0,0"
                          Content="Show research radars"
                          IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.ShowResearchRadars, Mode=TwoWay}"
                          ToolTipService.ToolTip="Show research/test radar markers such as KCRI (ROC test bed, Norman OK)"/>
            </Grid>
        </Expander>

        <!-- The home site is PICKED in the Radar Atlas (where you can see what you're choosing); this only
             shows it and holds the one launch preference. -->
        <Expander Grid.Row="1" Header="Home site" IsExpanded="True"
                  Style="{StaticResource SectionExpanderStyle}">
            <Grid RowSpacing="8">
                <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- current home -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- load on launch -->
                </Grid.RowDefinitions>

                <TextBlock Grid.Row="0" Margin="4,0,0,0"
                           Text="{x:Bind ViewModel.SiteFavorites.HomeSiteSummary, Mode=OneWay}"
                           Foreground="{ThemeResource TextFillColorSecondaryBrush}"/>

                <!-- PERSISTED (AppSettings.LoadHomeOnLaunch), default off. -->
                <CheckBox Grid.Row="1" Margin="4,0,0,0"
                          Content="Load home site on launch"
                          IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.SiteFavorites.LoadHomeOnLaunch, Mode=TwoWay}"
                          ToolTipService.ToolTip="Start the live radar loop for your home site when Anvil opens"/>
            </Grid>
        </Expander>

        <!-- READOUTS - how a measurement is SPOKEN, not what is drawn. One setting so far; it is a section
             rather than a loose row because the next one of its kind (UTC vs local times) lands beside it. -->
        <Expander Grid.Row="2" Header="Readouts" IsExpanded="True"
                  Style="{StaticResource SectionExpanderStyle}">
            <Grid RowSpacing="4">
                <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- distance unit -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- what it covers -->
                </Grid.RowDefinitions>
                <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

                <TextBlock Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="0" Margin="4,0,12,0"
                           VerticalAlignment="Center" Text="Distance"/>

                <!-- A SegmentedPicker, not a ComboBox: three fixed options, and the whole set is worth
                     seeing at once. PERSISTED (AppSettings.DistanceUnits) and pushed into the map page,
                     which formats the ruler's own chip and tick labels itself. -->
                <prim:SegmentedPicker Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="1"
                                      HorizontalAlignment="Left" Width="280"
                                      ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.DistanceUnitLabels}"
                                      SelectedIndex="{x:Bind ViewModel.DistanceUnitIndex, Mode=TwoWay}"/>

                <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" Grid.ColumnSpan="2"
                           Margin="4,2,0,0" TextWrapping="Wrap" MaxWidth="420"
                           HorizontalAlignment="Left" Opacity="0.75"
                           Text="Ground distances - the range ruler's readout and its range labels. Heights and wind-profile levels stay in kilometres."/>
            </Grid>
        </Expander>

        <!-- RANGE RINGS & RULER - the PREFERENCES behind the scope furniture and the tools tier's Ruler key
             (arming it is a gesture and stays on the tier). One section because they are one object: the ruler
             ends ON the reflectivity ring and wears its colour, so recolouring one without the other would read
             as two unrelated marks.
             ⚠️ WHICH RINGS is a set-once preference (the CLAUDE.md placement test), so it lives here and not on
             the tools tier. The page SIZES the reflectivity and velocity rings from the frame on screen
             (radar-scope.js); these rows only choose which are drawn. Distance rings speak the READOUTS unit —
             there is deliberately no second unit setting — and the ruler still ends at the reflectivity
             reach with that ring switched off.
             ⚠️ The checkbox swatches are literal copies of theme.css's DARK ring colours — they identify the
             line, they don't restyle it, so they're DATA brushes like ColorSwatchPicker's chips.
             ⚠️ The anchor's "My location" is kept even with no location marker placed - the ruler measures
             from the site meanwhile and its chip says so. Don't grey the segment: a preference you set before
             dropping a marker should simply start working when you drop it.
             ⚠️ Colour is PRESETS (Models/Radar/ScopeColors explains why not a free picker). A = the theme's
             own, and the only one that adapts to the light theme. The sweep pulse keeps its own colour. -->
        <Expander Grid.Row="3" Header="Range rings &amp; ruler" IsExpanded="True"
                  Style="{StaticResource SectionExpanderStyle}">
            <Grid RowSpacing="8" ColumnSpacing="12">
                <Grid.RowDefinitions>
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- rings -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- distance spacing -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- anchor -->
                    <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- colour -->
                </Grid.RowDefinitions>
                <Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="Auto"/>
                    <ColumnDefinition Width="*"/>
                </Grid.ColumnDefinitions>

                <TextBlock Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="0" Margin="4,6,0,0"
                           VerticalAlignment="Top" Text="Rings"/>
                <StackPanel Grid.Row="0" Grid.Column="1" Spacing="0">
                    <CheckBox IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.ShowReflectivityRing, Mode=TwoWay}"
                              ToolTipService.ToolTip="Where the radar's reflectivity data ends on the frame you're viewing">
                        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8">
                            <Rectangle Width="18" Height="2" VerticalAlignment="Center" Fill="#FF9FE0FF"/>
                            <TextBlock Text="Reflectivity reach"/>
                        </StackPanel>
                    </CheckBox>
                    <CheckBox IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.ShowVelocityRing, Mode=TwoWay}"
                              ToolTipService.ToolTip="Where velocity data ends. Past it there is no velocity or storm-relative velocity">
                        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8">
                            <Line X1="0" Y1="0" X2="18" Y2="0" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                  Stroke="#FFFFA07A" StrokeThickness="2" StrokeDashArray="2,1.5"/>
                            <TextBlock Text="Velocity reach"/>
                        </StackPanel>
                    </CheckBox>
                    <CheckBox IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.ShowDistanceRings, Mode=TwoWay}"
                              ToolTipService.ToolTip="Evenly spaced rings for judging distance from the radar, in your distance unit">
                        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8">
                            <Line X1="0" Y1="0" X2="18" Y2="0" VerticalAlignment="Center"
                                  Stroke="#FFC7CDD4" StrokeThickness="1" StrokeDashArray="1,3"/>
                            <TextBlock Text="Distance rings"/>
                        </StackPanel>
                    </CheckBox>
                </StackPanel>

                <TextBlock Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="0" Margin="4,0,0,0"
                           VerticalAlignment="Center" Text="Spacing"/>
                <prim:SegmentedPicker Grid.Row="1" Grid.Column="1"
                                      HorizontalAlignment="Left" Width="240"
                                      ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.DistanceRingSpacingLabels}"
                                      SelectedIndex="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.DistanceRingSpacingIndex, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                      IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.ShowDistanceRings, Mode=OneWay}"
                                      ToolTipService.ToolTip="How far apart the distance rings are, in your distance unit (Readouts). Auto picks a step to suit the radar's reach"/>

                <TextBlock Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="0" Margin="4,0,0,0"
                           VerticalAlignment="Center" Text="Ruler from"/>
                <prim:SegmentedPicker Grid.Row="2" Grid.Column="1"
                                      HorizontalAlignment="Left" Width="240"
                                      ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.RulerAnchorLabels}"
                                      SelectedIndex="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.RulerAnchorIndex, Mode=TwoWay}"
                                      ToolTipService.ToolTip="Where the range ruler starts: the radar site, or your location marker (the site until one is placed)"/>

                <TextBlock Grid.Row="3" Grid.Column="0" Margin="4,0,0,0"
                           VerticalAlignment="Center" Text="Colour"/>
                <prim:ColorSwatchPicker Grid.Row="3" Grid.Column="1" HorizontalAlignment="Left"
                                        ItemsSource="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.ScopeColorSwatches}"
                                        ToolTips="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.ScopeColorNames}"
                                        SelectedIndex="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.ScopeColorIndex, Mode=TwoWay}"/>
            </Grid>
        </Expander>

    </Grid>
</UserControl>
